<!-- page.hbs -->
{{!< default}}
{{#post}}
<article class="gh-article {{post_class}}">
    {{#match @page.show_title_and_feature_image}}
    <header class="gh-header gh-canvas">
        <h1 class="gh-title">{{title}}</h1>

        {{#if custom_excerpt}}
            <p class="gh-excerpt">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>
        {{/if}}

        {{#if feature_image}}
            <figure class="gh-feature-image">
                <img src="{{feature_image}}" alt="{{#if feature_image_alt}}{{feature_image_alt}}{{else}}{{title}}{{/if}}" />
                {{#if feature_image_caption}}
                    <figcaption>{{feature_image_caption}}</figcaption>
                {{/if}}
            </figure>
        {{/if}}
    </header>
    {{/match}}

    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        body {
            font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
            line-height: 1.6;
            color: #4a4a4a;
            background-color: #faf9f7;
        }
        .container {
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 60px 20px;
        }
        h1 {
            font-size: 2.5em;
            color: #8b6f47;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            font-weight: 600;
        }
        h2 {
            font-size: 1.5em;
            color: #8b6f47;
            margin-top: 30px;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }
        p {
            margin-bottom: 15px;
            text-align: justify;
        }
        ul {
            margin-left: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }
        li {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }
        .timeline {
            background-color: #f4f1ed;
            padding: 20px;
            border-left: 4px solid #8b6f47;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        .contact-box {
            background-color: #fffbf5;
            border: 2px solid #8b6f47;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 20px 0;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        .condition-list {
            background-color: #faf9f7;
            padding: 15px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            border-left: 4px solid #c99a6e;
        }
    </style>

    <div class="container">
        <h1>Returns & Refunds Policy</h1>

        <h2>1. Right to Return</h2>
        <p>
            We want you to be completely satisfied with your purchase from Aunty Suzy. If you're not happy with your purchase for any reason, we offer a 14-day returns window from the date you receive your order.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Returns Window</h2>
        <div class="timeline">
            <p><strong>Returns Period:</strong> 14 days from delivery date</p>
            <p>Items must be returned within this period to be eligible for a refund. Returns received after 14 days cannot be accepted.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>3. Condition of Returns</h2>
        <p>
            Items must be returned in the following condition to be eligible for a full refund:
        </p>
        <div class="condition-list">
            <ul>
                <li>Unused and in original, unworn condition</li>
                <li>In original packaging where applicable</li>
                <li>With all tags and labels attached</li>
                <li>Clean and undamaged</li>
                <li>Not personalised or custom-made (unless defective)</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <h2>4. Non-Returnable Items</h2>
        <p>
            The following items cannot be returned for refund:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Personalised or bespoke items (made to order)</li>
            <li>Items that show signs of wear or damage due to customer use</li>
            <li>Food items (for hygiene and safety reasons)</li>
            <li>Digital products or downloads</li>
            <li>Items returned without original packaging</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. How to Return an Item</h2>
        <p>
            To initiate a return, please follow these steps:
        </p>
        <ol style="margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 15px;">
            <li>Contact us at returns@auntysuzy.co.uk within 14 days of delivery</li>
            <li>Provide your order number and reason for return</li>
            <li>We'll send you return instructions and a returns address</li>
            <li>Pack the item securely and post it back to us</li>
            <li>Once received and inspected, we'll process your refund</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>6. Return Shipping</h2>
        <p>
            You are responsible for the cost of return shipping unless the item is faulty or damaged on arrival. We recommend using a tracked delivery service. Once we receive and inspect your item, we'll process your refund within 7-10 working days.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Faulty or Damaged Items</h2>
        <p>
            If your item arrives faulty, damaged, or not as described, please contact us immediately with photographs. We will cover the cost of return shipping and will either send you a replacement or issue a full refund, whichever you prefer.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Refund Process</h2>
        <p>
            Once we receive your return and confirm it meets our returns criteria, we will process your refund within 7-10 working days. The refund will be credited to your original payment method. Please allow 5-10 working days for the funds to appear in your account, depending on your bank.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Exchanges</h2>
        <p>
            We don't offer direct exchanges, but you can return an item and place a new order for a different product. If there's an issue with sizing, please contact us and we may be able to help.
        </p>

        <div class="contact-box">
            <h3 style="color: #8b6f47; margin-bottom: 10px;">Need Help?</h3>
            <p><strong>Email:</strong> returns@auntysuzy.co.uk</p>
            <p><strong>Response time:</strong> Within 2 working days</p>
            <p style="margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.95em;">Please include your order number and as much detail as possible when contacting us about a return.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>10. Consumer Rights</h2>
        <p>
            The above terms are in addition to your statutory consumer rights. If you believe you have a fault with an item, you may be entitled to remedies under the Consumer Rights Act 2015. For more information, visit the Citizens Advice website or contact Trading Standards.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="gh-content gh-canvas">
        {{content}}
    </div>
</article>
{{/post}}